From 34031a4ebd206b8542b73ee718cfeff0c8d08223 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Brue <ryanbrue.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 14:08:23 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: arm: cpus: add the mediatek,mt8173-smp enable
 method

On MT8173 boards whose firmware does not ship ARM Trusted Firmware, PSCI
CPU_ON sets a secondary core's entry point but leaves its MTCMOS power
domain off, and CPU_OFF parks the core but leaves the domain on. The kernel
has to power the domain itself around the PSCI calls. Document the enable
method that does so, for arm64 alongside psci and spin-table.

Boards that do ship ARM Trusted Firmware keep using "psci"; BL31 powers the
domain for them.

Signed-off-by: Ryan Brue <ryanbrue.dev@gmail.com>
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/arm/cpus.yaml | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/arm/cpus.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/arm/cpus.yaml
index 5be89c584..380b89355 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/arm/cpus.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/arm/cpus.yaml
@@ -244,6 +244,9 @@ properties:
       - enum:
           - psci
           - spin-table
+          # PSCI CPU_ON/CPU_OFF wrapped with the CPU MTCMOS power sequence
+          # the firmware omits (MT8173 boards without ARM Trusted Firmware)
+          - mediatek,mt8173-smp
       # On ARM 32-bit systems this property is optional
       - enum:
           - actions,s500-smp
